{"type": "root", "attrs": {"index": "no"}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Clustering smoke and pyro simulations"], "extent": [12, 54]}, {"type": "summary", "indent": 0, "text": ["Creates a clustered (partitioned) pyro simulation with multiple containers, using the selected point geometry as sources. This is useful for large or sparse sources, and for distributing simulations to a farm."], "extent": [54, 273]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Overview"], "extent": [273, 288], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "em", "text": ["Clustering"]}, " partitions a large or sparsely-distributed smoke or pyro\nsimulation into multiple (possibly overlapping) fluid boxes instead of one\ngiant box."], "extent": [288, 446]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": [{"scheme": "Image", "value": "/images/dynamics/clustering1.png", "type": "img", "text": ""}], "extent": [446, 488]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Using multiple small boxes has several advantages:"], "extent": [488, 540]}, {"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": ["Can be distributed to multiple processes and/or machines on a farm."], "extent": [540, 611]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": ["Solves faster since the computer doesn\u2019t have to deal with the empty spaces\nbetween the important parts of the overall simulation."], "extent": [611, 745]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": ["The small boxes can be much higher resolution, or multiple resolutions,\nwhereas a giant box usually must have a lower resolution because of memory\nlimitations."], "extent": [745, 908]}], "container": true}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["The multiple containers created by these tools are ", {"type": "em", "text": ["separate simulation\nobjects"]}, " with ", {"type": "em", "text": ["no interaction between each other"]}, ". For example, density cannot\nmove out of one container into an adjacent one. This is usually not a problem\nfor smoke and fire simulations."], "extent": [908, 1171]}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Creating a clustered smoke/pyro simulation from point sources"], "extent": [1171, 1239], "body": [{"type": "ord_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Select the object you want to emit from."], "extent": [1239, 1284]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["On the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Pyro FX"]}, " shelf tab, click ", {"scheme": "Icon", "value": "SHELF/smokecluster", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/pyro/SHELF/smokecluster.html"}, " Smoke Cluster\nor ", {"scheme": "Icon", "value": "SHELF/pyrocluster", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/pyro/SHELF/pyrocluster.html"}, " Pyro Cluster."], "extent": [1284, 1405], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["The tool creates a new network named ", {"type": "code", "text": [{"type": "var", "text": ["objectname"]}, "_sourcpts"]}, "."], "extent": [1405, 1476]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["The new network contains a ", {"scheme": "Icon", "value": "SOP/scatter", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/pyro/SOP/scatter.html"}, {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/sop/scatter", "type": "link", "text": ["Scatter"], "fullpath": "/nodes/sop/scatter.html"}, "\n    node that creates points on the input geometry\u2019s surface."], "extent": [1476, 1617]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["These points are then partitioned by a ", {"scheme": "Icon", "value": "SOP/clusterpoints", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/pyro/SOP/clusterpoints.html"}, "\n    ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/sop/clusterpoints", "type": "link", "text": ["Cluster Points"], "fullpath": "/nodes/sop/clusterpoints.html"}, " surface node. The clustering\n    branches off into nodes operating on the ", {"type": "q", "text": ["instance points"]}, " (the points that\n    will emit smoke/fire) and ", {"type": "q", "text": ["cluster points"]}, " (the points on which the\n    containers will be centered)."], "extent": [1617, 1951]}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["On the ", {"type": "q", "text": ["instance point"]}, " branch it creates a ", {"scheme": "Icon", "value": "SHELF/convert_to_fire", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/pyro/SHELF/convert_to_fire.html"}, "\n    ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/sop/pyrosource", "type": "link", "text": ["Pyro Source"], "fullpath": "/nodes/sop/pyrosource.html"}, " and ", {"scheme": "Icon", "value": "SOP/attribnoise", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/pyro/SOP/attribnoise.html"}, "\n    ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/sop/attribnoise", "type": "link", "text": ["Attribute Noise"], "fullpath": "/nodes/sop/attribnoise.html"}, " nodes to set appropriate values for\n    the necessary point attributes, which are then rasterized into volumes."], "extent": [1951, 2255], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": [{"scheme": "Image", "value": "/images/dynamics/clustering_sops.jpg", "type": "img", "text": ""}], "extent": [2255, 2309]}], "container": true}, {"blevel": 6, "type": "bullet", "indent": 4, "text": ["In the DOP network, the tool creates a regular ", {"scheme": null, "value": "pyro", "type": "link", "text": ["pyro setup"], "fullpath": "/pyro/pyro.html"}, ". On the\n    ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/dop/smokeobject", "type": "link", "text": ["Smoke object"], "fullpath": "/nodes/dop/smokeobject.html"}, ", it turns on\n    ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Create Objects From Points"]}, " (in the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Instancing"]}, " tab) and imports the\n    cluster points from the geometry network."], "extent": [2309, 2567]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["To change the number of containers, in the geometry network select the\n", {"scheme": "Icon", "value": "SOP/clusterpoints", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/pyro/SOP/clusterpoints.html"}, {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/sop/clusterpoints", "type": "link", "text": ["Cluster Points node"], "fullpath": "/nodes/sop/clusterpoints.html"}, " and modify\nthe ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Clusters"]}, " parameter."], "extent": [2567, 2750]}], "container": true}]}, {"level": 1, "id": "related", "container": true, "type": "related_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [2750, 2759], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": [{"scheme": null, "value": "/render/batch", "type": "link", "text": ["Distributed rendering"], "fullpath": "/render/batch.html"}], "extent": [2759, 2801]}], "container": true}], "text": "Related"}], "title": ["Clustering smoke and pyro simulations"], "summary": ["Creates a clustered (partitioned) pyro simulation with multiple containers, using the selected point geometry as sources. This is useful for large or sparse sources, and for distributing simulations to a farm."]}